    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0720" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">412.00/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-09T14:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1919, 2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 10, 2.10
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2081. Secretary of Mexican Claims Commission today stated that the total amount
                    of claims presented as mentioned in Embassy’s telegram 2065 April 26, 2 p.m.
                    included only claims presented to the commission now in session, but that claims
                    to the extent of approximately 43,000,000 pesos had been presented to the former
                    claims commission<anchor n="18" xml:id="d596-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0721" n="636" xml:id="pg636"/> for damages suffered during the Madero
                    revolution and that all these claims have been taken over by the new
                    commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
